<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FBType Name="AD_TO_AR" Comment="Composite FB for converting AD (DWORD) adapter to AR (REAL) adapter — ⚠&#10;BIT-REINTERPRETATION, NOT a numeric cast! A raw counter/analog value is&#10;misinterpreted as IEEE754 bits. See AD_TO_AR_TODO.md / AD_TO_AR_NUM for the safe&#10;two-stage (bit-string-&gt;int-&gt;real) alternative.">
	<Identification Standard="61499-2" Description="Copyright (c) 2026 HR Agrartechnik GmbH  &#10; &#10;This program and the accompanying materials are made  &#10;available under the terms of the Eclipse Public License 2.0  &#10;which is available at https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/  &#10; &#10;SPDX-License-Identifier: EPL-2.0">
	</Identification>
	<VersionInfo Organization="HR Agrartechnik GmbH" Version="1.0" Author="Franz Höpfinger" Date="2026-02-17">
	</VersionInfo>
	<CompilerInfo packageName="adapter::conversion::unidirectional">
	</CompilerInfo>
	<InterfaceList>
		<Plugs>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="AR_OUT" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::AR" Comment="REAL Adapter Output" x="2300" y="0"/>
		</Plugs>
		<Sockets>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="AD_IN" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::AD" Comment="DWORD Adapter Input" x="0" y="0"/>
		</Sockets>
	</InterfaceList>
	<FBNetwork>
		<FB Name="Convert" Type="iec61131::conversion::F_DWORD_TO_REAL" x="1000" y="0">
		</FB>
		<EventConnections>
			<Connection Source="AD_IN.E1" Destination="Convert.REQ" dx1="100"/>
			<Connection Source="Convert.CNF" Destination="AR_OUT.E1" dx1="100"/>
		</EventConnections>
		<DataConnections>
			<Connection Source="AD_IN.D1" Destination="Convert.IN" dx1="100"/>
			<Connection Source="Convert.OUT" Destination="AR_OUT.D1" dx1="100"/>
		</DataConnections>
	</FBNetwork>
	<Attribute Name="eclipse4diac::core::TypeHash" Value="''"/>
	<Attribute Name="Documentation" Type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<h1>AD_TO_AR</h1>

<h2>🇩🇪 Deutsch</h2>

<p><strong>⚠️ Achtung:</strong> Dieser Baustein wandelt DWORD nicht numerisch in REAL um, sondern nutzt intern <code>F_DWORD_TO_REAL</code>, was im FORTE-Kern für Bit-String-Quelltypen (BYTE/WORD/DWORD/LWORD) eine reine IEEE754-Bit-Reinterpretation ist. Ein roher Zähler-/Analogwert wie <code>DWORD#2048</code> wird dadurch NICHT zu <code>REAL#2048.0</code>, sondern zu einer bedeutungslosen Zahl nahe Null.</p>

<p><code>AD_TO_AR</code> ist trotzdem korrekt und sinnvoll, wenn <code>AD_IN</code> bereits ein Bitmuster ist, das als REAL interpretiert werden soll (z. B. das Ergebnis von <code>F_REAL_TO_DWORD</code> oder ein anderweitig serialisiertes Float).</p>

<p><strong>Für einen echten Zahlenwert</strong> (z. B. Analog-Rohwert, Zähler) siehe stattdessen <code>AD_TO_AR_NUM</code> im selben Ordner — gleiche Schnittstelle, aber numerisch korrekt (Kette DWORD→UDINT→REAL).</p>

<h2>🇬🇧 English</h2>

<p><strong>⚠️ Warning:</strong> This block does not numerically convert DWORD to REAL — it internally uses <code>F_DWORD_TO_REAL</code>, which in the FORTE core is a pure IEEE754 bit-reinterpretation for bit-string source types (BYTE/WORD/DWORD/LWORD). A raw counter/analog value such as <code>DWORD#2048</code> will NOT become <code>REAL#2048.0</code>, but a meaningless value near zero.</p>

<p><code>AD_TO_AR</code> is still correct and useful when <code>AD_IN</code> is already a bit pattern meant to be interpreted as REAL (e.g. the result of <code>F_REAL_TO_DWORD</code>, or otherwise serialized float data).</p>

<p><strong>For an actual numeric value</strong> (e.g. raw analog value, counter), use <code>AD_TO_AR_NUM</code> in the same folder instead — same interface, but numerically correct (DWORD→UDINT→REAL chain).</p>
]]></Attribute>
</FBType>
